      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-130274",
      ":question/problem": "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-2).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(x,y)=(2,-2)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,-2).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(2,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}))i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}))j \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}})}{1+{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{1+{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}}\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-2) & =-\\frac{(-2)}{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{8}\\,i+\\frac{2}{8}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(i+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(2,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(2,-2)}{‖∇f(2,-2)‖} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}(i+j)}{‖\\frac{1}{4}(i+j)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}(i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+j).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
